1.2 How components communicate
1.  EA to backend: HTTPS, signed telemetry. Each message has an instance ID, mode, sequence, timestamps, and a signature. Rejected messages are logged.
2.  Backend to EA: signed commands, pulled by the EA over HTTPS. Each command has an expiry and a class (N, R, or A). The EA verifies the signature, identity, expiry, and sequence before acting.
3.  Backend to Firestore: writes through a privileged service identity. Browsers never write trading records.
4.  Dashboard to Firebase: reads status through the Firebase client SDK under security rules. Phase 1 is read-only.
5.  Dashboard to backend: authenticated API calls for permitted requests only. In Phase 1, the command path is disabled.
6.  TradingView to backend: alert webhook with a shared secret. Readiness information only.
7.  Brains to Decision Engine: in-process calls in the backend. If Brains are moved out of the backend later, they use the same authenticated channel.
8.  EA to broker: standard MT5 trade and history functions, through the terminal.
Rule: no component communicates with the EA except through the signed command channel or the signed telemetry channel. Firestore is not a command channel.
