7. Strategy research and validation
Status: no strategy has a proven edge. No backtest has been run. All three candidates are unselected. The protocol below is APPROVED in principle as the research method described in V3 and V4, with the details below PROPOSED for approval. Selection criteria are UNRESOLVED until written and approved before any test.
7.1 Candidates (specifications to be written and approved)
• A. Trend-Aligned Pullback: M15 direction, pullback definition, M5 confirmation, M1 entry, invalidation, stop, target, regime suitability.
• B. Breakout and Retest: defined breakout, closing confirmation, retest, failed-breakout rule, trigger, invalidation, stop, target. May depend on pending orders (CS-8).
• C. Liquidity Sweep and Reversal: liquidity level from Brain 04, sweep definition, reclaim, structure and displacement confirmation, trigger, invalidation, stop, target.
Each specification is a fixed written document in research/specs/, with a version. A specification cannot change after results are seen without a new version and a note of why.
7.2 Specification template (every strategy)
1.  Market and timeframes.
2.  Each condition, with its exact rule and the Brains it uses.
3.  Entry trigger and order type (market or pending).
4.  Stop-loss rule and minimum distance handling.
5.  Take-profit or exit rule.
6.  Position size rule within the risk limit.
7.  Filters: session, volatility, news window.
8.  Invalidation and expiry rules.
9.  Parameters, with ranges and the default used in the first test.
10.  Known limits and the conditions in which the strategy should not trade.
7.3 Data
• Source for historical tests: MT5 Strategy Tester with recorded tick history from the broker (NOT VERIFIED for depth and quality).
• Any external data is recorded separately with its source and licence.
• Data quality checks before use: gaps, duplicated bars, spread outliers, weekend and holiday handling.
• The data set, its date range, and its checksum are recorded in the test configuration.
7.4 Cost model (same for all three candidates)
• Spread: from recorded broker spread data, not a fixed assumption, where data exists.
• Commission: from the Exness Standard schedule, verified at setup (NOT VERIFIED).
• Swap: from the broker's specification (NOT VERIFIED).
• Slippage: stated assumption, varied across a range in sensitivity tests.
• Costs are reported separately so their effect on results is visible.
7.5 Comparison protocol
1.  Fix the date ranges and splits before running any test: in-sample, out-of-sample, and rolling walk-forward windows.
2.  Include periods of trend, range, and high volatility. Report which periods are covered.
3.  Run each candidate under the same data, costs, and risk limits.
4.  Log every parameter set tried. The count is reported with results, because a large number of trials raises the chance of a false result.
5.  Report for each candidate: net expectancy per trade with a confidence interval, profit factor, maximum drawdown and recovery, trade count, win and loss distribution, and sensitivity to each cost assumption.
7.6 Out-of-sample and walk-forward validation
• Out-of-sample: parameters chosen on in-sample data are tested once on out-of-sample data. Re-tuning after seeing out-of-sample results is recorded as a new trial.
• Walk-forward: repeated optimisation on a window, tested on the next window, rolled forward. The stability of parameters across windows is reported.
• A strategy whose results depend on one period or one parameter value is reported as inconclusive.
7.7 Robustness and overfitting checks
• Parameter neighbourhood: results should not collapse for small parameter changes.
• Cost stress: results at higher spread and slippage.
• Trade-count floor: a minimum trade count is set before testing. Below it, results are inconclusive.
• Randomised or shuffled tests where the method allows, to check that results are not produced by noise.
7.8 Demo testing
• Demo forward evaluation is a Phase 3 activity, 8 to 12 weeks, on the broker DEMO account.
• It runs only after Phase 2 approval and only through the full EA path.
• Its results are reported separately from any backtest. Backtest and demo results are never merged.
7.9 Selection criteria
UNRESOLVED. The Founder must approve the criteria before any test begins. Recommended structure: a minimum trade count; a minimum out-of-sample expectancy with a positive lower bound on its confidence interval; drawdown within a limit set by the Founder; results stable across walk-forward windows; results that survive the cost stress. A candidate that meets all criteria may proceed to demo. A candidate that meets none is not selected. If no candidate meets the criteria, the outcome is recorded as no strategy selected.
7.10 What the research can and cannot show
• It can show whether a rule set produced a particular result on particular data under stated costs.
• It cannot prove future profitability, live fills, or execution quality.
• A selected candidate, if any, is still subject to demo testing and to a separate Founder decision.
7.11 Records
Each run writes: specification version, data set reference, cost model, parameters, trial count, metrics, and the selection outcome. Stored under research/results/ and copied into the Strategy Lab view with its source label.
