• Reproducibility: the same configuration run twice gives the same results.
• Data checks: gaps and duplicates detected on known bad data.
• Cost sensitivity: results recomputed under stressed costs.
• Split discipline: out-of-sample data not used for parameter choice; check by log.
• Trial count recorded and reported.
• Pass criterion: all checks recorded. Passing these checks does not mean a strategy is profitable.
